From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Null IDE Build <build@nullide.local>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] feat: inject Null custom stylesheet into workbench HTML

Adds a <link> for null-custom.css after the main workbench stylesheet.
The source lives at workbench/custom.css in the overlay repo and is copied
to src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/null-custom.css before the gulp
build runs (see "Copy workbench CSS" step in build.yml), so it ends up
alongside workbench.html in the packaged artifact.

The existing CSP already contains style-src 'self' and 'unsafe-inline',
so same-origin stylesheets load without any policy change.
---
 src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html b/src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html
index a1b2c3d..e4f5a89 100644
--- a/src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html
+++ b/src/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@
 	"/>

 		<!-- Workbench CSS -->
 		<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../workbench/workbench.desktop.main.css">
+		<link rel="stylesheet" href="null-custom.css">
 	</head>

 	<body aria-label="">
